A||||9||Scott2M4||HELP!  Some sort of electrical problem!?||||4
Z||000000||Scott2M4||11-10-1999||01:03 AM||||Last night, I replaced the spark plugs, valve cover gasket, auto belt tensioner and serpentine belt on my '87 4cyl coupe.  After the work was done, I took it for a test drive - everything seemed perfect!  It ran smoother and quieter than ever!  Decided it was cool to drive it home (I was working on it in a garage about 20 minutes away).<P>As I got close to home, the dash lights seemed to get dim.  I thought it was just my eyes so I ignored it.  As I coasted to a stop shortly thereafter, the dash idiot lights lit up, the gauge lights (minus the radio lights) got very dim and the engine died.  Turning the key produced NOTHING!  The temperature guage was sitting just above the first line.<P>I was able to bump start the car but it ran very rough and, by the time I reached my driveway, people were flashing their lights because they couldn't see me with my almost unlit headlights.<P>Prior to the work I did last night, I had an intermittent problem where the battery light would flash and the turn signals would not!  I also had complaints with how dark the dash lights were at night - even with the adjustment dial cranked all of the way up!<P>What does this sound like to you folks?  A battery, an alternator, a voltage regulator?  How much in $$$ am I looking at?  I've only had the car a week and it's already putting a strain on my marriage!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Help, please!!!!!||||reg||4
Z||000001||sinoloa||11-10-1999||02:27 AM||||Go to AutoZone or a parts store where they have a battery tester. They can tell you how much life your battery has left on it, and its cheaper than replacing the battery all together.  It sounds like a battery problem to me.  If they test the battery while its on the car, they can tell you if its the battery or the alternator.||||reg||10
Z||000002||sinoloa||11-10-1999||02:29 AM||||Autozone can test the battery for free.  Sometimes places will charge you a few dollars.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||11-10-1999||08:37 AM||||It sounds more like a dieing alternator to me.  As it fails to keep the battery charged you will start to lose power to everything electrical, including the fuel pump.<BR>Give the battery a good charge and see if everything works as usual.  <P>Autozone will need the battery to have a good charge in order to load test it.  They can do this for you but it will take a while.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DJRice||11-10-1999||09:50 AM||||The regulator is built in to the alternator, and this problem sounds like an alternator problem.<P>Verify that you didnt bump any of the plugs while you were working on the topside, and if everything is ok, pull the alt and have it tested.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ChadMan||11-10-1999||10:07 AM||||My guess would be alternator as well.  When I bought my 86 SE, sometimes I'd be driving along A-OK, then suddenly the voltage reading would drop to 12 and the "VOLTS" light would come on.  A few miles down the road, the needle would spring back up to 14 and the light would go out.  A new alternator cured the problem.  It was $80 at NAPA, but might be cheaper at Auto Zone, Advance, etc.<P>Check your chassis grounds and battery cables, too.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||sdm1964||11-10-1999||09:46 PM||||I had the same problem on my 85 GT, low dash lights, alt light on dimly. I pulled the alt took it to the parts store and had it tested for free. The diode trio was bad, replaced with new brushes too, rebuild kit cost $13.00 at discount auto parts. Mine was an 94 amp alt.<BR>good luck||||reg||1
Z||000007||Scott2M4||11-11-1999||06:48 AM||||FIXED!  Two hours, a "new" (reconditioned) alternator and a recharged battery later, the car is on the road again!<P>This forum is GREAT!  Is there anything you all can't do!!!???||||reg||1
Z||000008||Scott2M4||11-11-1999||06:48 AM||||FIXED!  Two hours, a "new" (reconditioned) alternator and a recharged battery later, the car is on the road again!<P>This forum is GREAT!  Is there anything you all can't do!!!???||||reg||1
Z||000009||DJRice||11-11-1999||10:26 AM||||Well, I cant speak for anyone else, but I cant seem to win Lotto....||||reg||8
